<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman–Safavid wars</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ottoman-Safavid wars, Safavid-Ottoman rivalry</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottoman–Safavid wars were a series of conflicts between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the Shi'a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> from the sixteenth to the eighteenth century. They were fought over eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. The rivalry institutionalised the Sunni–Shi'a divide as a geopolitical fault line in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a>.</p></div>
